ASSUMPTIONS.md:3:Conservative choices where the Omarchy / Quickshell / Hyprland API was not 100% certain. The rule: isolate the uncertainty behind a small adapter, prefer documented types (`Process`, `Socket`, `FileView`, `IpcHandler`, `PanelWindow`), and degrade.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:7:- **Entry points are `Item`s**, not `ShellRoot`. Overlay exposes `open(payloadJson)` / `close()` / `toggle()` for `omarchy-shell shell summon|hide|toggle`. Taken from the Quattro shell README and the Desktop Undo overlay.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:8:- **`keepLoaded: true`** is set on the manifest even though the spec JSON block omitted it. The platform reference says plugins that must outlive a single summon (this overlay) should set it. Spec kinds/entryPoints are otherwise exact.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:10:- **Settings are inline on the `shell.json` plugins[] entry.** Service declares `roots`, `watchCap`, `cacheMb`, `maxFiles`, `extraExclude` only. The host copies those fields onto the Item; they flow to the helper via a `config` command *before* indexing starts. There is no nested `pluginSettings` object and no plugin-owned settings file. Runtime UI state (`firstRunShown`) is `~/.local/state/quicklook/ui.json`, not a settings file.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:11:- **Service owns the only helper.** Overlay never launches `quicklookd`. It talks to the warm service over documented `omarchy-shell shell call <id> <method> <arg>` (`query` / `preview` / `prefetch` / `snapshot` / …). There is no `pluginRegistry.serviceFor` or in-process `shell.summon`. Persistent and one-shot helper launches pass `--plugin-dir <pluginDir>` so the demo corpus is not resolved from the shell cwd.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:12:- **IPC verb** is `omarchy-shell shell call <id> <method> <arg>` and `shell summon <id> <payloadJson>`. Every `IpcHandler` method takes the required string argument (empty when unused). README examples always pass `<arg>`. We do not write `hyprland.conf`.
ASSUMPTIONS.md:13:- **`IpcHandler` target** is the plugin id. Overlay polls `snapshot` and sends commands through that channel.
README.md:19:That is the whole cold path. The installer does not run build hooks. On first summon the overlay talks to the **service-owned** helper over `omarchy-shell shell call` (Python `compat/` when the Rust binary is missing). Invoice PDF pages rasterize through resource-limited `pdftoppm` when Poppler is installed; images over 20 MP are downsampled before QML sees them. No `build.sh` is required to get a working finder.
